                <pb facs="0811" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg703"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Gresham acknowledges receipt of Mr. Terrell’s telegram of the 15th, instructs
                    him to protest against punishment of Armenians who have become citizens of the
                    United States as criminals, as well as against their being imprisoned on any
                    ground for too long a time, although admitting that the Porte has the right to
                    expel them and, incidentally, to arrest them for the purpose of expulsion.</p>
            </div>
